<metadata><name>New England 100 (NAASA) 2026 - Published Courses</name><desc>Source: 2026 New England 100 Published Courses, as amended (Amendment 8/21: Course 9A G1 to starboard), NAASA, 21-22 Aug 2026. Start: line between the RC boat and an orange mark, in Potter's Cove - drawn at Potter Cove on the Jamestown side just north of the Newport Bridge (position approximate; the RC sets the line). Finish: line between the RC boat displaying an orange flag and R12, SW of Rose Island. Cautions: DO NOT SAIL BETWEEN THE NEWPORT BRIDGE AND ROSE ISLAND. Bridges are gates: Pell Newport Bridge under the 3 center spans, all other bridges under the center span. Round government marks within 10 boat lengths (not R12 or bridge supports). Coddington Cove / Coasters Harbor naval exclusionary zone is an obstruction. Courses 2 and 4: direction announced the morning of the race - drawn in one direction only. The RC may modify, shorten or add courses each morning. Points named (routing) only keep the drawn line in navigable water and are not marks of the course. Published distances are approximate; courses 6, 7, 8 and 9 measure well short of the published figure.</desc></metadata>
